These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.

- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
- A provider round that reports no usage does not poison the total: the rounds that reported are still counted, and a turn where no round reported passes `undefined` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
- Aggregation sums each token field of two reporting rounds ([validated by: sums each token field when both rounds reported](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L32)), keeps the reported side when only one round reported ([validated by: keeps the later round when the earlier round reported nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36); [validated by: keeps the earlier round when the later round reported nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)), and stays `undefined` when neither did ([validated by: stays undefined when neither round reported](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L44)).
  });
});

describe('addUsage', () => {
  const a = {inputTokens: 1, outputTokens: 2, totalTokens: 3};
  const b = {inputTokens: 10, outputTokens: 20, totalTokens: 30};

  it('sums each token field when both rounds reported', () => {
    expect(addUsage(a, b)).toEqual({inputTokens: 11, outputTokens: 22, totalTokens: 33});
  });

  it('keeps the later round when the earlier round reported nothing', () => {
    expect(addUsage(undefined, b)).toEqual(b);
  });

  it('keeps the earlier round when the later round reported nothing', () => {
    expect(addUsage(a, undefined)).toEqual(a);
  });

  it('stays undefined when neither round reported', () => {
    expect(addUsage(undefined, undefined)).toBeUndefined();
  });
});

